This repository is a new implementation in a different language. It changes
the original: it replaces the Windows UI with GTK4, uses Linux-native paths,
and changes the behaviour of several components. Where code or structure is
carried over from the original, it remains subject to the original license
and its copyright notices. Those notices belong to their respective authors.

This product is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. See LICENSE.

The rv-gtk AppImage (rv-gtk-x86_64.AppImage) bundles shared libraries of the system it was built
on (Ubuntu), copied unchanged: GTK 4, GLib/GObject/GIO, Pango, Cairo, gdk-pixbuf, HarfBuzz,
Graphene and their dependencies. Several of them are licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public
License (GTK 4, GLib, GObject, GIO, Pango, Cairo, gdk-pixbuf, HarfBuzz, librsvg, Graphene among
them) and the Adwaita icon theme under LGPL-3.0 or CC-BY-SA-3.0. Their copyright files and the
licence texts they refer to are inside the AppImage under usr/share/doc/<package>/ and
usr/share/doc/common-licenses/; usr/share/doc/rv-rs/bundled-packages.txt lists the packages.
The libraries are loaded as shared libraries and can be replaced by the user: extract the
AppImage with `./rv-gtk-x86_64.AppImage --appimage-extract`, change files in squashfs-root/usr/lib,
and run squashfs-root/AppRun. The source of each is available from the Ubuntu archive for the
package named there.
